    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d308">

                <pb facs="0446" n="350" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg350"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">894c.111/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Crane</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-01-03T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 3,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1. Your 432 [<hi rendition="#italic">434</hi>], December 14, 6 p.m.<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d308-f1"/></p>
                <p>You may notify Consuls that on and after January 15, our temporary acquiescence
                    in Japanese passport control on railways under Japanese supervision is
                    withdrawn. In view of request of Japanese Minister for postponement of this
                    notification you should inform him of your action in this matter stating that
                    this Government of course is unable to acquiesce in his contention that it did
                    not assent to these regulations inasmuch as this Government does not concede
                    that the Japanese authorities have been granted any right to scrutinize the
                    passports of American citizens in Chinese territory.</p>
                <p>With reference to your 343 of October 25, 5 p.m.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d308-f2"/>
                    You should inform your British colleague of the action which you have taken in
                    this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Davis</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
